<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Delcy Rodríguez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1969">1969</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Delcy Rodríguez is a Venezuelan lawyer and politician of the United Socialist Party of Venezuela, the daughter of the left-wing leader Jorge Antonio Rodríguez. She served as foreign minister, presided over the Constituent Assembly of 2017 and became vice-president under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicolas-maduro">Nicolás Maduro</a> in 2018; after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> forces seized Maduro in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caracas">Caracas</a> in January 2026, she assumed the presidency.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/delcy-rodriguez.jpg" alt="Delcy Rodríguez" width="320" height="403" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Presidency of Venezuela · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Delcy_Rodr%C3%ADguez_-_02_(19-01-2026)_(cropped_2)_(b).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
